// Outlets (DEC-034): the newspapers, broadcasters, and social platforms
// that decide what people hear. Generated when play begins: a town outlet
// for each town with its home place (the newspaper, DEC-079), one per region,
// one for the nation. Each has an audience by income class and age band, a
// reach, an editorial lean (an attitude vector drawn around its audience's
// views), a credibility, interests (concerns), finances, and journalists
// (the Named people with these occupations at its home place). Outlets
// choose stories by newsworthiness × interest × access and frame them by
// their lean; they never just repeat a politician.
